  "id": "campgiardia",
  "note": "CAMP GIARDIA: a camp on the pond shore that has stopped being temporary.\n\nThe tile's prose: tarpaulin over a bus shell, a cook fire in a cut-down drum, a hand-lettered\nboard reading CAMP GIARDIA, and a row of beans along the waterline that something has eaten.\n\nThe bus is the room, and it is a bus: a storey-high body sitting on its frame with the wheels gone,\na rounded roof, windows down both sides, and the door and the windscreen at the yard end, which\nis pulled up to the yard line. The tarp is ridged over its roof on a pole and pegged out on four\nmore, so there is a dry yard down one side, lit from the bus windows. The tail of the bus sticks out\nat the waterline end, because a tarp that hid the whole bus made the camp a beige slab from any\nheight, and the cook fire is a drum in the open beside it. The board stands on two posts at the\nyard. The bean canes run along the back, by the water.\n\nNothing is lit but the bus windows and the fire.\n\nThe tile is one storey (`flags.floors: 1`), so the bus spends most of `h` and the ridge all of it.\n\nIt stands in for the `campgiardia` arm (`replaces`), which stays in LEGACY_MODELS.",
  "pal": "ty_giardia_bus",
  "replaces": "campgiardia",
